    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22633" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γον-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>begetter, father</i>, mostly in pl., <i>parents,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Cer.
				240
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				235
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				6.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				178b
			</span></i>, etc.: in sg., of a serpent, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.109
			</span></i>; of a man, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				457d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φράζε τίνος γονέως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>).<i><span class="en">
				310
			</span></i>: generally, <i>progenitor, ancestor</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέμπτος γ.</span>
			<i>ancestor</i> in the fifth generation, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.91
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				8.32
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἄνωθεν γ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>GA</u>
					722a8
				</span></i>
			. (Nom. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γονεῖες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Histria</u>
					7.27
				</span></i>
			: acc. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γονέᾰς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					261
				</span></i>
			: dat. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γονεῖσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					1267.24
				</span></i>
			 (Ios, <span class="entity">iii A. D.</span>).)</div>
